      "term": "Rib in the round",
      "definition": "Working fpdc and bpdc alternately around a joined circle of stitches. Each stitch worked on the right side becomes the paired stitch on the next round, keeping the rib columns continuous."
    },
    {
      "slug": "crotch-split-g166",
      "term": "Crotch split",
      "definition": "The point where the single body tube is divided into two leg tubes. Chain a small bridge across the gap at the back crotch, then work each leg in rounds from there down to the ankle."
    }
